00:00:08.160 --> 00:00:14.760
Unit 6. Travel in Southeast Asia 2. How to be responsible travelers?

g11-audio-6-2
00:00:15.540 --> 00:00:26.280
Before making a trip, it's important to think about how you can be a responsible traveler and reduce the negative impact you may create on the environment.

g11-audio-6-3
00:00:26.280 --> 00:00:28.780
If so, what can you do?

g11-audio-6-4
00:00:29.580 --> 00:00:37.680
It's not always easy to be a responsible traveler, but it's necessary to keep a few things in mind.

g11-audio-6-5
00:00:38.660 --> 00:00:42.800
Here are five simple ways to be a responsible traveler.

g11-audio-6-6
00:00:43.440 --> 00:00:50.860
1. Buy local items A big part of a responsible traveler is supporting the local community,

g11-audio-6-7
00:00:51.280 --> 00:00:53.240
helping it to grow and flourish.

g11-audio-6-8
00:00:53.240 --> 00:01:05.420
One of the best ways to make a positive impact on the lives of the local people in the place you're visiting is to buy locally made handicrafts

g11-audio-6-9
00:01:05.420 --> 00:01:12.260
instead of those that have been shipped from continent to continent for thousands of miles.

g11-audio-6-10
00:01:13.180 --> 00:01:19.900
2. Watch your waste Every year, million tons of plastic end up in the oceans.

g11-audio-6-11
00:01:20.620 --> 00:01:27.800
Garbage on the beach and in the water looks ugly and is really harmful to marine life and the environment.

g11-audio-6-12
00:01:28.500 --> 00:01:38.380
A great way to help out with waste is to use reusable bags and containers and natural and plastic-free products.

g11-audio-6-13
00:01:39.680 --> 00:01:46.520
3. Save energy Taking a train or a bus is a much greener way to get around than taking a taxi.

g11-audio-6-14
00:01:46.520 --> 00:01:49.300
If you can, walk or cycle.

g11-audio-6-15
00:01:49.860 --> 00:01:54.680
If you have to take a taxi, try to share the ride with someone else.

g11-audio-6-16
00:01:54.980 --> 00:02:03.920
Other ways to save energy while traveling involve taking shorter showers, reducing your hot showers, adjusting your air conditioning,

g11-audio-6-17
00:02:04.420 --> 00:02:10.020
avoiding unnecessary washing and drying and turning lights off when not in use.

g11-audio-6-18
00:02:11.060 --> 00:02:21.220
4. Respect the culture and customs of local people It's also important to respect the culture and customs of the destinations you travel to.

g11-audio-6-19
00:02:21.720 --> 00:02:26.640
In many parts of the world, wearing shorts and t-shirts isn't appropriate.

g11-audio-6-20
00:02:27.220 --> 00:02:35.880
If you're visiting temples and religious monuments, make sure you're dressed according to the culture and customs of the local people.

g11-audio-6-21
00:02:37.220 --> 00:02:45.780
5. Visit less popular places In the world, some places have so many tourists that they have to limit the number of people.

g11-audio-6-22
00:02:46.340 --> 00:02:49.960
In some cases, they have to shut down some places.

g11-audio-6-23
00:02:50.540 --> 00:02:59.680
One thing you can do is to visit less popular places, it will help to balance out the number of tourists across the more popular destinations.

g11-audio-6-24
00:03:00.280 --> 00:03:05.440
You'll have a more enjoyable experience by not having to deal with crowded streets.

g11-audio-6-25
00:03:06.240 --> 00:03:09.260
Everyone can be a responsible traveler.

g11-audio-6-26
00:03:09.960 --> 00:03:17.000
As I've mentioned, there are many simple ways in which you can help out, the environment and the local people.
